3. Michelle Wong / Lab Muffin Beauty Science
--------------------------------------------
    data/corpus-labmuffin.json
    cache/extract-labmuffin.json    (see the warning at the end of this section)

Michelle Wong is a real person, a cosmetic chemist with a PhD, and she writes
Lab Muffin Beauty Science at https://labmuffin.com. Her ten most recent posts
were fetched once, by hand, from her public RSS feed on 2026-09-20 and used as a
real-world test that the extraction works on somebody we did not invent.

Her words are hers. They are not licensed to us and we are not relicensing them.

Because this repository is public, each article body in `data/corpus-labmuffin.json`
has been cut to roughly its first 200 characters. What remains is the title, the
link, the date, the image URLs and the typed attributes a vision model read off
those images. Anyone who wants the real corpus should re-fetch it themselves:

    python scripts/fetch_corpus.py rss https://labmuffin.com/feed/ --full
    python scripts/enrich_images.py labmuffin

Her photographs are referenced at their original labmuffin.com URLs and are
loaded from her server by the browser at display time. No image bytes from her
site are stored in this repository.

    WARNING, still outstanding: cache/extract-labmuffin.json embeds the SAME
    article bodies under its `corpus[].text` key, roughly 29,000 characters of
    them, because it is a frozen record of exactly what was sent to the model.
    Trimming data/corpus-labmuffin.json alone does not remove her prose from this
    repository. The frontend only reads the first sentence of each of those
    strings, so the same 200-character cut can be applied to the cache without
    changing what the demo shows.

If Michelle Wong would prefer not to appear here at all, that request wins over
anything in this file. Contact via labmuffin.com.


4. Jev and TypeSafe
-------------------
    docs/research/typesafe-http-api.md
    docs/research/jev-engineering-playbook.md

`typesafe-http-api.md` is a copy of TypeSafe's own published API reference,
compiled from docs.typesafe.ai on 2026-09-20 so the build could work offline. It
is TypeSafe's documentation, not ours. The canonical version is at
https://docs.typesafe.ai and should be preferred over this snapshot.

Jev is a TypeSafe System One model, used here over their public HTTP API under
their terms. No model weights are in this repository.


